Table agent_webhooks {
  id text [pk, not null]
  org_id text [not null]
  agent_employee_id text [not null]
  slug text [not null, unique]
  secret_hash text [not null]
  hmac_key_encrypted text [note: 'Per-webhook AES-encrypted HMAC key (fix #7). New webhooks issue this alongside the legacy scrypt secret so callers can sign with HMAC-SHA256 (`x-deft-webhook-signature: sha256=<hex>`) instead of shipping the raw secret. Pre-existing rows have NULL until they\'re rotated.']
  label text
  enabled boolean [not null]
  last_fired_at timestamp
  fire_count integer [not null]
  created_by text
  created_at timestamp [not null]
  updated_at timestamp [not null]
  indexes {
    (org_id) [name: 'agent_webhooks_org_idx']
    (agent_employee_id) [name: 'agent_webhooks_employee_idx']
  }
  Note: 'Block 3.3 — per-agent webhook URLs. An agent-employee can expose an HMAC-signed URL that accepts POST payloads from external systems. The dispatcher enqueues an employee-trigger with trigger_kind=\'webhook\' so the agent runs its playbook over the incoming payload.'
}

